PROJECT: REPORTING SCRIPTS AT TORT

## Overview
This project is a set of Python-based automation tools designed to (1) extract specific fund accounting data from a web application called Eagle, and (2) generate various (i) position reports for use by portfolio managers and (ii) regulatory reports for submission to clients and regulators

## Project Structure
The project is organised as follows:
- 'src\': contains the source code and main scripts
- '\requirements.txt': lists all dependencies to run the project elsewhere

## Prerequisites
- Python 3.x
- Git

## Installation

1.  **Clone the repository**
    ```bash
    git clone [https://github.com/hilton26/X.git](https://github.com/hilton26/X.git)
    cd X

2. **Set up the virtul environment** It is recommended to run this project in a virtual environment so that dependencies can be controlled
    ```bash

    # Windows
    python -m venv .venv
    .venv\Scripts\activate

    # Mac/Linux
    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv\Scripts\activate

3. **Install dependencies**
    ```bash
    pip install -r requirements.txt

** Usage
    To run the main script, ensure your virtual environment is active and run:
    ```bash
    python src/[script name].python

